00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:01.920
'cause smoke inhalation
for a short period of time

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.510
is rarely strong enough to
cause you to pass out instantly.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:08.430
The only way that could
happen is there's some kind of

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.590
chemical process going on,
like something burning,

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.180
causing a poison sensation.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.580
When you're around a fire,
there's a few things that

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:17.340
can happen that could cause
you to not get enough oxygen.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:20.730
A, fire essentially burns
and eats up off that oxygen

00:03:20.730 --> 00:03:22.260
so it can cause you to asphyxiate.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.750
Also when you're burning something,

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.670
you naturally create carbon monoxide,

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:29.790
which when you inhale, actually
binds with the hemoglobin

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.950
in your blood, which
normally carries oxygen

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:34.650
and competes with the oxygen
that you're also inhaling

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:37.200
to bind to that hemoglobin,
forming carboxyhemoglobin

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.720
and then that circulates
through your body,

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.210
not giving your tissues
the oxygen that it needs

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:45.090
and as a result, you can die
from carbon monoxide poisoning.

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:46.350
We've seen that time and time again

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:48.330
and the way to reverse
that is by giving a patient

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:53.160
a ton of oxygen to sort of
out-compete that carbon monoxide

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.840
that is already floating
around in the blood

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.070
trying to bind to the hemoglobin.

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.210
Another thing obviously that could happen

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:59.040
is a chemical burn of your trachea

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.120
and that's really problematic.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:01.213
You need a breathing tube for that.

